From e274d4bfcbb86c8b6cd48a9787ad1584436472dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon Mikuda <simon.mikuda@streamunlimited.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 17:43:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc2: gadget: NAK OUT endpoints until a request is
 queued

dwc2_hsotg_ep_enable() activates an OUT endpoint (USBACTEP) but sets
SNAK only for isochronous ones. A bulk or interrupt OUT endpoint is thus
active with NAK clear and no transfer programmed, and the core ACKs the
host's data for it into the shared RxFIFO. In buffer DMA mode there is
no DMA address to move that packet to, so it sits at the head of the
RxFIFO and every other OUT endpoint stops receiving until a request is
queued on this one.

On a Raspberry Pi Zero W with an NCM + ACM composite gadget this takes
the network down at every boot: the host (ModemManager) writes to the
ACM port as soon as it enumerates, nothing opens ttyGS0 on the device
until a getty starts, and in the meantime NCM receives nothing. When the
tty is finally opened the stuck packet drains, but the NCM transfer
behind it comes back with a wrong length ("Wrong NTH SIGN"), and by then
the host has timed out and aborted its transfers, so the link stays
dead.

Set SNAK whenever an OUT endpoint is enabled. dwc2_hsotg_start_req()
already clears NAK when it arms the endpoint, and the core sets NAK
again when a transfer completes, so an OUT endpoint only accepts data
while it has somewhere to put it.

Signed-off-by: Simon Mikuda <simon.mikuda@streamunlimited.com>
---
 drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c b/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c
index 102169b40419..d16e94e0a2a4 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c
@@ -4104,6 +4104,16 @@ static int dwc2_hsotg_ep_enable(struct usb_ep *ep,
 	 */
 	epctrl |= DXEPCTL_USBACTEP;
 
+	/*
+	 * NAK OUT tokens until a request is queued. An active OUT endpoint
+	 * with NAK clear accepts data into the shared RxFIFO even while it is
+	 * not enabled; in buffer DMA mode nothing takes that packet out of the
+	 * FIFO, so it blocks every other OUT endpoint until this one gets a
+	 * request. dwc2_hsotg_start_req() clears NAK when it arms the endpoint.
+	 */
+	if (!dir_in)
+		epctrl |= DXEPCTL_SNAK;
+
 	/* update the endpoint state */
 	dwc2_hsotg_set_ep_maxpacket(hsotg, hs_ep->index, mps, mc, dir_in);
 
@@ -4129,7 +4139,6 @@ static int dwc2_hsotg_ep_enable(struct usb_ep *ep,
 			mask |= DIEPMSK_NAKMSK;
 			dwc2_writel(hsotg, mask, DIEPMSK);
 		} else {
-			epctrl |= DXEPCTL_SNAK;
 			mask = dwc2_readl(hsotg, DOEPMSK);
 			mask |= DOEPMSK_OUTTKNEPDISMSK;
 			dwc2_writel(hsotg, mask, DOEPMSK);
-- 
